{"ratings":[{"id":"F1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An ignored dependency fixture containing a .git entry can cause the factory to refuse otherwise valid merges and rebases, blocking integration."},{"id":"F2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"unusual","reason":"Replacing a tracked file with a nested repository causes the factory to commit only the deletion, silently losing the replacement from the result."},{"id":"F3","consequence":"diag","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An unreadable checkout directory causes a safe refusal with a raw filesystem error instead of an explanation of the inspection failure."}]}